WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.272
OpenAI preprint disproves

00:00:02.083 --> 00:00:03.380
the polynomial Hirsch

00:00:03.192 --> 00:00:04.005
conjecture

00:00:04.518 --> 00:00:06.133
An OpenAI preprint

00:00:05.945 --> 00:00:07.725
constructs simple polytopes

00:00:07.572 --> 00:00:08.810
with n facets

00:00:08.657 --> 00:00:10.001
whose graph diameter

00:00:09.813 --> 00:00:11.027
grows faster than

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:12.076
any fixed power

00:00:11.888 --> 00:00:12.501
of n

00:00:12.737 --> 00:00:14.246
refuting the polynomial

00:00:14.058 --> 00:00:15.201
Hirsch conjecture

00:00:15.718 --> 00:00:16.932
The paper dated

00:00:16.744 --> 00:00:18.135
November 24

00:00:18.206 --> 00:00:19.043
shows that for

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:19.939
every sufficiently

00:00:19.751 --> 00:00:21.024
large facet count

00:00:20.836 --> 00:00:21.413
there is a

00:00:21.225 --> 00:00:22.734
bounded simple rational

00:00:22.546 --> 00:00:24.444
polytope of subpolynomial

00:00:24.256 --> 00:00:24.963
dimension

00:00:25.093 --> 00:00:26.343
whose vertex graph

00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:27.557
has superpolynomial

00:00:27.369 --> 00:00:28.182
diameter

00:00:28.718 --> 00:00:30.251
The repository includes

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:31.111
the Lean statements

00:00:30.923 --> 00:00:32.208
for the refutation

00:00:32.043 --> 00:00:33.010
and the paper's

00:00:32.822 --> 00:00:34.059
two main theorems

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:35.604
Full story on

00:00:35.415 --> 00:00:36.311
the dashboard
